<div id="all" class="docs-page">
    <div id="basicinfo" class="docs-body">
        <h2>Stack in one paragraph</h2>
        <p>
            No framework - just Node's <code>node:http</code> plus a small OOP core you can read
            in an afternoon. Pages are EJS templates (plain HTML with
            <code>&lt;%= variable %&gt;</code> holes) that compile once at boot and auto-escape
            every interpolated value, so XSS-safe output is the default. Data lives in two SQLite
            files accessed through Drizzle ORM with a Prisma-style query surface. Client scripts are
            TypeScript built twice: ES5 plus polyfills for IE11, and an ES2015 bundle for modern
            browsers.
        </p>

        <h2>Where things live</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><b>server.ts</b> - boot + page routes; the only wiring file</li>
            <li><b>src/core/</b> - the framework: application pipeline, router, context, sessions, cache, static server, security, errors, views</li>
            <li><b>src/routes/</b> - API endpoints grouped by site area, all guarded + rate-limited</li>
            <li><b>src/views/</b> - .ejs templates; shared chrome in partials/</li>
            <li><b>src/styles/</b> - CSS sources; design tokens and light/dark themes</li>
            <li><b>src/lib/db/</b> - Drizzle schemas + query clients (main.db = tech tools, web.db = SaaS)</li>
            <li><b>src/server/queries/</b> - data access used by routes</li>
            <li><b>src/client/</b> - browser scripts, compiled to ES5 and ES2015 at build</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Commands</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><code>pnpm run dev</code> - watchers: TS server reload + client rebuild on save</li>
            <li><code>pnpm run build</code> - everything lands in dist/ (server, views, assets)</li>
            <li><code>pnpm start</code> - production serve from dist/</li>
            <li><code>pnpm run check</code> - types + lint + audit</li>
            <li><code>pnpm test</code> - unit tests</li>
            <li><code>pnpm run check:views</code> - render every template with sample data</li>
            <li><code>pnpm run check:full</code> - check + tests + views + hot reload</li>
            <li><code>pnpm run parity</code> - diff rendered pages vs frozen legacy baselines</li>
            <li><code>pnpm run format</code> - Prettier (EJS templates excluded)</li>
            <li><code>pnpm run db:migrate</code> - generate SQL migrations from schema changes</li>
            <li><code>pnpm run db:reset</code> - recreate dev databases with seed data</li>
            <li><code>pnpm run setup</code> - create or rotate the operator account from environment variables</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Themes &amp; payments</h2>
        <p>
            One <code>theme</code> cookie drives both sites. The server stamps
            <code>data-theme</code> on the root element, so the chosen theme survives a reload and
            never flashes. Payments run through Stripe in USD; PayPal and Bitcoin stay disabled
            until server-side verification exists.
        </p>

        <h2>Sessions &amp; auth</h2>
        <p>
            Cookies are HMAC-signed (<code>v1.payload.signature</code>) verified with
            <code>timingSafeEqual</code>. Authorization is re-read from the database per request - editing
            the session cookie changes nothing.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

